course: dictionary
lesson: 1373
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Cap» can mean a hat, a lid or a limit, so the words around it tell you which meaning the writer means. Read the clues first, then choose.
explain: «She put on her red cap before the sun got hot.» A hat goes on your head, and the sun is a clue, so cap means a hat here. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Put the cap back on the bottle.» Bottles have lids, so this cap is the small lid. Slang can work the same way: if a friend says «no cap», the words around it tell you they mean they are telling the truth.
fact: Cap is a noun (cap, caps) and a verb (cap, caps, capped).
fact: A cap is a soft hat, often with a peak at the front, like a baseball cap or a sun cap.
fact: A cap is also a small lid on a bottle, a pen or a tube, like «the cap on a pen».
fact: In sport, a cap is a place in a national team. To cap something means to put a limit or top on it.
fact: «No cap» is slang meaning no lie, for real. In French, un chapeau is a hat and une casquette is a cap.
exercise: «She put on her red cap before going out into the sun.» What is a cap here? | A place in the national team | A limit on how much you can spend | A small lid on a bottle | *A soft hat with a peak at the front
exercise: «Please put the cap back on the bottle.» What does this mean? | Put the team in order | *Put the lid back on the bottle | Put a limit on the money | Put a hat on your head
exercise: «The council decided to cap the price of tickets at ten pounds.» What does cap mean here? | *To put a limit on something | To wear a hat | To put a lid on a bottle | To win a place in the team
test: «He was picked for his country and won his first cap.» In sport, what is a cap? | A small lid on a bottle | A limit on the price of tickets | *A place in the national team | A soft hat
test: Jo says «no cap, I saw it myself». What does no cap mean? | The price has a limit | The lid is missing | There is no hat on the head | *No lie, it's really true
exam: «The cap came off the bottle and the juice spilled.» Which meaning of cap fits here? | A soft hat | *A small lid | A limit or top | A place in the team
